Pre-filled syringes are drug delivery systems supplied with a predetermined dose of medication in a ready-to-use syringe. By combining drug storage and administration in a single device, these systems can reduce preparation steps, improve dosing accuracy, and support more convenient treatment delivery.

They are used across a range of therapeutic areas, including vaccination, autoimmune disease management, and other treatments requiring injectable medicines. Their adoption is supported by the expansion of biologic therapies, increased demand for reliable drug delivery, and the growing role of home-based healthcare.

The market encompasses syringe components, complete delivery systems, and related manufacturing technologies. Glass remains an important material because of its established use in pharmaceutical packaging, while polymer-based designs offer alternative characteristics for selected applications. Manufacturers must ensure that syringe materials remain compatible with drug formulations and meet stringent sterility, quality, and safety requirements.

